{"id": "EUVD-2026-86630", "enisaUuid": "af4381fc-eddc-3c61-b533-ca0ca020ee3b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: validate packet_len before skb_put_data\n\nbtintel_pcie_submit_rx_work() reads packet_len from rfh_hdr without\nchecking if it exceeds the RX buffer size. An oversized packet_len\ncan lead to an out-of-bounds read in skb_put_data().\n\nValidate packet_len to ensure it is non-zero and does not exceed\nBTINTEL_PCIE_BUFFER_SIZE - sizeof(*rfh_hdr), logging an error when\ninvalid.\n\nThis issue was reported by Claude Mythos. It can be simulated either by\nusing customized firmware configured to return an invalid packet_len or\nby modifying rfh_hdr->packet_len in the driver before calling\nbtintel_pcie_submit_rx_work().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab0159b1f7214ce9bad9862751e4553e635a21b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73a50c636425cb9f7ab647b5a97bd14dd5610076", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46884c0f92708f1d218fc94d88800227a19b52f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6436e1b5331b1aebf905c13e0880a37032719b75"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97976", "GHSA-wxpf-g955-mjcc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b338460-7118-36b8-a2cd-791618a627c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "40a71cc8-397e-389c-8eb5-6f4a0deac2e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4c96f760-1eb9-368b-9f86-b9721ed8ebed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "7134de05-ae83-3feb-a777-a62f7b2c0ecd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "8cbe3e68-3b5f-3d7a-a389-e69d09cd291e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a5639c42-cd34-3674-9f54-d04ec16c1170", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <46884c0f92708f1d218fc94d88800227a19b52f8"}, {"id": "b94b13de-bdf4-372f-a6da-19af54d389d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "bd5f6b66-396a-3636-a379-12e0c0c5898b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <6436e1b5331b1aebf905c13e0880a37032719b75"}, {"id": "cf5c1e1b-f870-39d2-9061-7e8309c66bb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <73a50c636425cb9f7ab647b5a97bd14dd5610076"}, {"id": "e5cf4309-3864-3dd6-8027-f703dad35f71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <ab0159b1f7214ce9bad9862751e4553e635a21b1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d712fd78-7a13-32ed-a3ab-d3496c831706", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}